  <conditions attached="1">
   <condition type="2">
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Cote d&apos;Ivoire Regional Compact may be suspended or terminated, among other conditions, if Cote d&apos;Ivoire (i) fails to comply with its commitments under the agreements entered into with MCC in relation to the program, (ii) engages in a pattern of actions inconsistent with the criteria used by MCC to determine eligibility for the program, or (iii) engages in activities contrary to the national security interests of the United States. Disbursements of funding under a Compact Program are subject to specific conditions set forth in the Compact Program agreement for the individual projects funded thereby, as well as general conditions, such as the delivery of implementation, fiscal accountability, and monitoring and evaluation plans.</narrative>
   </condition>
